# Phase 7: example Caddy config for the optional `caddy` compose
# service (profile "https"). Caddy gets automatic HTTPS (Let's Encrypt)
# for free from just a domain name - no manual cert/CA setup needed.
#
# Copy to `Caddyfile` (git-ignored, may contain your real domain) and
# edit the domain:
#   cp Caddyfile.example Caddyfile
#
# Already running Traefik/nginx/another reverse proxy for this host?
# Skip the `caddy` compose service entirely and just point your
# existing proxy at the `gateway` container's published port
# (127.0.0.1:8000, see docker-compose.yml) instead of adding a second
# one - one HTTPS terminator per host is enough.

mcp.example.com {
	reverse_proxy gateway:8000
}
